# The scenes of the feature-flags deck, in order. Each "## Scene N: title" is one slide, spoken with item N of
# feature-flags.narration.md. Each line under a heading puts one thing on the slide:
#   note "<text>"         a line of text
#   show <file> ...       a code panel: <from> <to> or /pattern/, then a label; --mark and --zoom mark lines
#   run_live "<command>"  a live run, played from its cast in feature-flags.outputs/
#   callout "<text>"      a boxed sentence saying what a result means

## Scene 1: step 1, the version catalogue
note "Step 1: add the OpenFeature SDK to the version catalogue."
show libs.versions.toml "/openfeature/" gradle/libs.versions.toml

## Scene 2: step 2, the dependency
note "Step 2: add it to the lesson. The code itself asks the flag, so it is a main dependency."
show lessons/feature-flags/example/build.gradle.kts "/^dependencies/" "lesson build file" --zoom 9

## Scene 3: the checkout and its flag
note "The checkout asks a *flag* which shipping rules to use: the old ones, or the new ones."
show Checkout 18 21 "the checkout" --zoom 19

## Scene 4: the code under test
note "The code under test: today's *new* shipping rules, behind the flag."
show TodaysNewShipping 8 14 "today's new rules" --zoom 8

## Scene 5: tests with the default flag
note "Tests that never set the flag: they only run the *old* rules."
show DefaultFlagsTest 11 18 "tests with the default flag" --zoom 13

## Scene 6: tests both ways
note "Tests that run *both ways*: the same checks with the flag off, then on."
show BothWaysTest 12 20 "tests both ways" --zoom 13-15
show Checkouts 29 43 "setting the flag" --mark 31-33,39,42

## Scene 7: both ways finds the bug
note "Run the tests against today's new rules:"
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:feature-flags:test -Pcode=today"
callout "With the flag on, a €20 basket ships free: the threshold is in euros, compared with cents."

## Scene 8: the fixed new rules
note "The new rules, comparing cents with cents:"
show NewShipping 8 14 "the fixed new rules" --zoom 8
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:feature-flags:test"
callout "Both ways agree. Now the flag can be switched on, and later the old rules removed."
